(and when that was dead, he would be free. It would kill this monstrous) Tj
T* (soul-life, and without its hideous warnings, he would be at peace. He) Tj
T* (seized the thing, and stabbed the picture with it.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (There was a cry heard, and a crash. The cry was so horrible in its) Tj
T* (agony that the frightened servants woke and crept out of their rooms.) Tj
T* (Two gentlemen, who were passing in the square below, stopped and looked) Tj
T* (up at the great house. They walked on till they met a policeman and) Tj
T* (brought him back. The man rang the bell several times, but there was no) Tj
T* (answer. Except for a light in one of the top windows, the house was all) Tj
T* (dark. After a time, he went away and stood in an adjoining portico and) Tj
T* (watched.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (?Whose house is that, Constable?? asked the elder of the two gentlemen.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (?Mr. Dorian Gray?s, sir,? answered the policeman.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (They looked at each other, as they walked away, and sneered. One of) Tj
T* (them was Sir Henry Ashton?s uncle.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Inside, in the servants? part of the house, the half-clad domestics) Tj
T* (were talking in low whispers to each other. Old Mrs. Leaf was crying) Tj
T* (and wringing her hands. Francis was as pale as death.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (After about a quarter of an hour, he got the coachman and one of the) Tj
T* (footmen and crept upstairs. They knocked, but there was no reply. They) Tj
T* (called out. Everything was still. Finally, after vainly trying to force) Tj
T* (the door, they got on the roof and dropped down on to the balcony. The) Tj
T* (windows yielded easily?their bolts were old.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (When they entered, they found hanging upon the wall a splendid portrait) Tj
T* (of their master as they had last seen him, in all the wonder of his) Tj
T* (exquisite youth and beauty. Lying on the floor was a dead man, in) Tj
T* (evening dress, with a knife in his heart. He was withered, wrinkled,) Tj
T* (and loathsome of visage. It was not till they had examined the rings) Tj
T* (that they recognized who it was.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (THE END) Tj
